				<div id="essay">
					<h2>Pitching in to help her team</h2>
					<p>On the pitcher&#8217;s mound is where Hannah&#8217;s qualities of talent, hard work, dedication, leadership, and passion truly shine.</p>
					<p class="pullquote">Hannah always holds her head high because she knows that she has given it her all.</p>
					<p>At the age of nine, Hannah&#8217;s parents signed her up for softball. She learned which hand to put her glove on, how to throw, and how to catch, but even more importantly, she discovered the world of pitching.</p>
					<p>Over the past two years, Hannah&#8217;s dedication has increased. She attends practice four days a week and pitches every evening in her basement or backyard, even throwing at lunch with her school&#8217;s athletic director. She has mastered two new pitches this year and can throw a ball with pinpoint accuracy at 45 miles per hour.</p>
					<p>Leadership takes many forms, and it is in this area that Hannah shows extremely honorable qualities. One year, she led her all-star team to victory by pitching more than 25 innings in one weekend. But what set her apart was the final game where she gave up the mound to her teammate&#8212;who had faced challenges all weekend&#8212;to deliver the final pitch for the victory.</p>
					<p class="last">All the games have not ended so glamorously. There have been many times when the trophies and medals have been given to others. Hannah has walked off the field knowing the taste of defeat. However, Hannah always holds her head high because she knows that she has given it her all, and that knowledge allows her to radiate with the glow that comes from knowing that she tried, that she did her best, and that she is a true winner.</p>
				</div>
